---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How Bra Sizes Work: The Complete Guide | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Understand how bra sizes work. Learn the relationship between underbust band numbers, bust cup letters, and relative volume capacity."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/guides/how-bra-sizes-work"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Guides', url: '/#guides' },
      { label: 'How Bra Sizes Work' }
    ]} />

    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Evergreen Guide
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        How Bra Sizes Work: The Complete Guide
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-xs text-mute mb-4">
        <span>By BraSizeChecker Editorial Team</span>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <time datetime="2026-08-24">Updated August 2026</time>
      </div>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        A bra size is a two-part code consisting of a <strong>band number</strong> (e.g. 34) and a <strong>cup letter</strong> (e.g. C). Understanding how these two components work together is the key to finding a supportive fit.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">1. The Band Number: Your Foundation</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The band number represents your underbust torso measurement in inches (30, 32, 34, 36, 38, 40). The band is designed to anchor against your ribcage and provide <strong>80% of your bra's total structural support</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">2. The Cup Letter: Relative Difference</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Contrary to popular belief, a cup letter is not a fixed volume. A cup letter represents the mathematical difference between your full bust measurement and your band measurement:
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl text-center mb-4 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink">
          Difference = Bust Measurement - Band Measurement
        </div>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li>1 inch difference = A cup</li>
          <li>2 inches difference = B cup</li>
          <li>3 inches difference = C cup</li>
          <li>4 inches difference = D cup</li>
          <li>5 inches difference = DD cup</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">3. Interactive Tools & Next Steps</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Now that you understand the mechanics of bra sizing, put it into practice:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
          <a href="/#calculator" class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl hover:border-accent text-center font-bold text-xs text-primary">Calculate Size &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/sister-size-calculator" class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl hover:border-accent text-center font-bold text-xs text-primary">Sister Size Tool &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/how-to-measure" class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl hover:border-accent text-center font-bold text-xs text-primary">Measurement Guide &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
